1. Add the following lines to your preamble (before `\begin{document}`):

```latex
\usepackage{tocloft} % optional: provides additional customization options for the TOC
\usepackage{titlesec} % optional: provides additional customization options for section headings

% Customize the appearance of section headings (optional)
\titleformat{\section}
  {\normalfont\Large\bfseries}{\thesection}{1em}{}

% Generate the TOC
\newcommand{\generateTOC}[1]{%
  \tableofcontents
  \clearpage
  \addcontentsline{toc}{section}{#1}
  \markboth{#1}{#1}
  \begin{center}
    \textbf{\large #1}
  \end{center}
  \clearpage
}

% Set the main TOC title
\newcommand{\mainTOCtitle}{Table of Contents}
```

2. Use the `\generateTOC{<title>}` command wherever you want to generate a TOC with a custom title. For example:

```latex
\chapter{Introduction}
\section{Overview}
\subsection{Background}

% Generate a TOC for the current chapter
\generateTOC{Chapter 1: Introduction}

\section{Objectives}
\subsection{Research Questions}

% Generate a TOC for the current section
\generateTOC{Section 1.2: Objectives}

\chapter{Literature Review}
\section{Related Work}
\subsection{Methodology}

